<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5316" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭfŏris</span></b> , e
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭfŏrus</span></b> ,
			a, um, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 4, 6 <i>fin.</i></span></i>),
			adj.
		bis-foris. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Having two doors</i> or <i>folding-doors</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">valvae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					2, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fenestrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. P.
					3, 3, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Having two openings</i> or <i>holes</i>, <i>double</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">via (narium),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 1</span></i>
			.—<b>Poet.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ubi assuetis biforem dat tibia cantum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 9, 618</span></i>
			 (bisonum, imparem, Serv.); <i><span class="en">Aus. Cent.
				Nupt. 27</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">biforis tumultus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 668</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
